    "uses_service": 0,
    "misc_details": "The buttons are arranged in a flattened pentagon shape, with the point on the bottom.  The throw button is the bottom point, above that are the two forward buttons, and the two back buttons on the top.  The original CP used the throw button also as the start; Mame has a seperate \u0027start\u0027 button, but both mame\u0027s \u0027throw\u0027 and \u0027start\u0027 buttons throw and start.  Mame labels the five buttons a little differently than the original CP: \u0027throw\u0027, \u0027R Paddle Forward\u0027, \u0027L Paddle Forward\u0027, \u0027L Paddle Backward\u0027, and \u0027R Paddle backward\u0027."
